id: pm-runner-ancestor-tracker
title: Reject external test scratch roots beneath an initialized ancestor tracker
description: "The test runner rejects scratch roots inside this checkout but admits external roots beneath a different initialized tracker. Fixtures that intentionally unset PM_PATH then discover that ancestor; nested init can update its settings. Reject every such root before fixture allocation, build, or child execution, including physical symlink aliases and root-layout trackers."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-08T04:43:08.875Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-08T05:32:02.650Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-08T05:32:01.950Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-08T05:32:01.950Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Initialized standard and root-layout ancestor trackers are refused before child execution; unrelated settings and uninitialized directories remain supported; failure diagnostics identify the unsafe root.
parent: pm-u9d0
resolution: "The runner checks physical temporary-root ancestry for standard and root-layout trackers before allocation, build or child execution; recurrence-family v2 registers the historical boundary and current checks."
expected_result: Discovery fixtures cannot reach a real ancestor tracker when PM_PATH is intentionally absent; unrelated valid settings remain supported.
actual_result: "Real standard/root ancestor controls fail before and pass after the guard; 46 runner unit cases and three integration cases pass, with complete 100/100/100/100 source coverage. The prior external initialization-settings incident is preserved and recorded; no guessed restoration is claimed."
